// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

// Script Variable Greeting :
// Script Variable Leave :

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Dialog - Desdemona 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Page DesdemonaIntro Text :
"P3275335896" "It is good to see you again, {HeroName}, though I wish I could say it were under better circumstances."
// Answer Text :
"P3863243824" "What's wrong? Where is everyone?"
// Answer Text :
"P1052625404" "The firewall... Malaise... is down. What's next?"
// Answer Text :
"P1450605698" "Penelope has been freed from Tilman's control. I presume that Mother Mayhem is next?"
// Answer Text :
"P3937593367" "Tilman's mind is loose in the network. We must disconnect her."
// Answer Text :
"P1330288503" "We must confront Malaise. Please, help us into the Network."
// Answer Text :
"P2528853983" "We are ready to rescue Penelope Yin. Please, open the portal."
// Answer Text :
"P599612011" "We are ready to save Aurora Borealis. Can you open the way?"
// Answer Text :
"P3177265069" "Shalice Tilman has retreated into Malaise. Open the portal and we'll finish this."
// Answer Text :
"P2471800980" "I guess this just leaves Tyrant, then?"
// Answer Text :
"P3407800810" "How is it that you're unaffected by the Mindwashing?"
// Page DescriptionStageOne Text :
"P1462876967" "After the broadcast at TPN Campus, Tyrant found himself with quite a restless populace. I admit I was quite surprised by the scale of the uprising that he was facing down. I guess the people of this world didn't take to kindly to learning that the devourer of their world was not quite as defeated as was let on!<br><br>It looked like the broadcast may actually have had the desired effect, but then... something... happened. People started to quiet their protest and return to their homes. At first it was small... one person, then another. Soon, whole mobs, then whole city blocks. The whole protest just stopped, with everyone abandoning the energy and vigor they had shown moments before.<br><br>It didn't stop with the protesters, however. This wave of passivity passed through the city and then onto the whole of the world.<br><br>It took some time before I found any others who were unaffected, and even then, our numbers are few. We have, however, found the cause."
// Answer Text :
"P428063320" "What was the cause of this sudden change?"
// Page DescriptionStageOne-PartTwo Text :
"P3118223545" "You may remember the technology Mother Mayhem developed called Mindwashing? It was used against you in the BAF and at TPN? Well, it turns out that, when she became Incarnate, Shalice Tilman, who inhabits the body of Aurora Borealis... known to you as Mother Mayhem... gained the ability to spread her mind through more than one body. With this power, Tilman was finally able to overwhelm the resistance of Penelope Yin. The combined psychic power of Tilman, Yin and Borealis was sufficient for her to propel the Mindwashing effect across all of Praetoria.<br><br>We are too few in number to do anything more ourselves. Mother Mayhem has fortified the hospital with a psionic energy field I cannot break through. A physical assault and confrontation is simply not in the cards.<br><br>We have found another way, however. With the help of Metronome, I have devised a ritual which will enable me to open a portal into the Seer Network. You will then be able to enter and deal with Shalice Tilman within her own domain."
// Answer Text :
"P868611843" "Inside the Seer Network? How is that even possible?!"
// Page DescriptionStageOne-PartThree Text :
"P3856476505" "The Seer Network is a strange amalgamation of magic and science. Within its wires and terminals and databases exists an alternate universe, where the minds of all those who fall under Mother Mayhem's spell are linked together. Within the Network, that which seems impossible even in our worlds is possible, and within the Network, Shalice Tilman's mind reigns supreme. So long as she remains connected to the Network, she is unstoppable, for she can just jump from one mind to another.<br><br>If we're to save Praetoria from this fate, we need to get into the Network and cut Tilman's connections to it. Before that can happen, however, we'll need to get through her firewall, Malaise, and then kick her out of the minds of the psychics she controls."
// Answer Text :
"P2534239813" "Malaise? What does he have to do with this?"
// Page DescriptionStageOne-PartFour Text :
"P681235306" "Mother Mayhem is not a fool. She knows that Incarnates like you would be likely to resist Mindwashing, no matter how powerful she became. Given that, she also knows that it would only be a matter of time before you devised some way to get at her.<br><br>Malaise is how she intends to counter you. He stands astride every access node to the deeper reaches of the Network where Penelope and Mother Mayhem hide. He waits, watching and ready for you. I have seen his presence for myself as I have gazed through the portal.<br><br>If this effort is to get anywhere, Malaise must be eliminated."
// Answer Text :
"P2097862093" "I see. So, take down Malaise and we can go after Tilman?"
// Answer Text :
"P3152589868" "How come you are unaffected?"
// Page DescriptionStageTwo Text :
"P3088305259" "Well, we're going to have to kick Shalice Tilman's mind out of the two psychics she currently possesses: Penelope Yin and Aurora Borealis. Aurora's buried pretty deep within the Network, so Metronome is going to help me better pinpoint her location.<br><br>Penelope, however... that node is a mess. For as strong as Mother Mayhem has gotten, Penelope is fighting her every step of the way. This continual struggle manifests as a titanic psychic storm which envelops Penelope's mind. While it made it easier to find where she is located, it also means her node is going to be very dangerous.<br><br>Still, you're not going to be going in without help. I'll still back you up with my awakening ritual from here, but Metronome also thinks he may be able to help. He's seeding the node now with some attractor code or some such, which he says will help. You can ask him more about it if you like, or, if you're ready, I can open the way in."
// Answer Text :
"P432648754" "We are ready to rescue Penelope Yin."
// Page DescriptionStageThree Text :
"P585322552" "With Penelope Yin freed, Tilman has had no choice but to retreat to Aurora's Mind. Fortunately, Metronome was able to track Tilman's retreat, so we've located the node in which Aurora Borealis has been imprisoned. All you need to do now is get in there and drive Tilman out of Aurora as well. Once we do that, it should be a fairly simple matter to disconnect her from the network.<br><br>In fact, chasing her out of Aurora Borealis is going to be the hard part. Aurora's mind is so repressed that it is effectively imprisoned, waiting silently, fearfully for that day when Tilman finally decides to kill her outright and possess the body fully.<br><br>With Tilman trapped like this, I fear that day may have come. You are almost certainly going to need to find some way to keep Aurora alive despite Tilman's best efforts to kill her."
// Answer Text :
"P1016176092" "We are ready to save Aurora Borealis."
// Answer Text :
"P491648670" "What will happen to Penelope Yin now?"
// Page PenelopeFateStageThree Text :
"P3030928042" "I'm currently locking on to Penelope Yin's physical location now, and I should be able to teleport her out to safety. Teleporting her out will be quite strenuous and attention-getting, however, so I would prefer to wait until Tilman is chased from Aurora. That will let me bring both Penelope and Aurora out of the network at the same time. The last thing I want to do is draw more attention to our location than I have to, so if I can just do the one ritual and recover both, it'll be better for us all."
// Answer Text :
"P3317188523" "Bring Penelope out when you can. We are ready to save Aurora Borealis."
// Page DescriptionStageFour Text :
"P3105492319" "Yes... we weren't really expecting that. Though, I guess there's always room for that to happen when you're dealing with disembodied minds wandering through some strange magical/scientific network.<br><br>I do think this may be her last stop, though. Malaise, even in his shattered state, was the only entity left in the whole network strong enough to be able to contain Shalice Tilman's mind. If you can manage to chase her mind out of his long enough, you should be able to disconnect her from the Seer Network.<br><br>Beyond that, I cannot really say much. We're in really uncharted territory here. All I can do is wish you luck and let you know that I will be backing you up from here as best as I can."
// Answer Text :
"P2442099980" "We are ready to put an end to Shalice Tilman."
// Page BattleStageOne Text :
"P4291818922" "Indeed. Malaise must be defeated before you can have any hope of reaching Tilman.<br><br>I will open the portal now. It will remain open for you and your allies to enter at your leisure. Just make sure you are ready for anything, and step through when you are prepared."
// Answer Text :
"P3631375107" "Thank you, Desdemona."
// Page BattleStageTwo Text :
"P4261181699" "Just remember: there is a massive psychic storm in the area. Make sure you have spoken to Metronome, so you can be sure of what he's going to do to help you!<br><br>Now, give me a moment and the way will be opened."
// Page BattleStageThree Text :
"P1061452545" "OK. Whatever you do, make sure Aurora stays alive! We don't need Tilman getting full control of anyone, especially not the body which she has made her home in for all this time!<br><br>Now, excuse me a moment while I open the way."
// Page BattleStageFour Text :
"P2242316116" "Very well then. I shall open the way. The rest is up to you."
// Page DesdemonaEnding Text :
"P3116652299" "I certainly hope so, yes. I'm growing quite tired of this world. The faster we can get him and the Praetorian Hamidon dealt with, the sooner we can return to Primal Earth and start planning to deal with the real threat.<br><br>I, for one, look forward to having the resources of Praetoria and its people at our disposal to assist us in the wars ahead."
// Answer Text :
"P938333489" "You do realize you're pretty important here, right?"
// Answer Text :
"P2793748414" "Sounds like a plan. See you then, Desdemona."
// Page DesdemonaEnding2 Text :
"P55519399" "What? Why would you say...<br><br><color goldenrod>Desdemona looks down, as if you've forced her to admit something she'd rather not.</color><br><br>Look, I know people are looking to ME to lead them now. The Carnival Mistresses haven't exactly been subtle about it. Believe me, I know... and with Calvin Scott being an utter nutcase....<br><br>This is NOT what I signed up for when I agreed to come here."
// Answer Text :
"P27698909" "You do have help here, you know."
// Answer Text :
"P373020419" "Well, sorry about that, Desdemona. Good luck."
// Page DesdemonaEnding3 Text :
"P1515417895" "Maybe. Neither Penelope or Aurora are quite their selves just yet and Metronome, while brilliant, kind of worries me a bit. What's to stop him from just going on a rampage?<br><br>I don't know... maybe they're all going to be a big help. But if they're not, I'm not sure I can be what everyone's expecting me to be."
// Answer Text :
"P2575544138" "You will do fine, Desdemona. I'm glad that I can count on you to assist us finish the job."
// Answer Text :
"P739110561" "Enough with the whimpering. Pull yourself together. We have a job to do."
// Page DesdemonaEnding4-Kind Text :
"P2321230339" "Well, I... Thank you for the vote of confidence. It's not something I've heard in quite some time.<br><br>OK, enough with that, I can do this. I will do this.<br><br>Whenever you need my help, whatever dimension you're in, feel free to call on me and my allies. We'll do everything we can."
// Page DesdemonaEnding4-Tough Text :
"P2953676237" "Whimpering? I do not whimper! I... Well, OK, that was a bit whiny. Is this what happens when you become good?<br><br>Anyway, you're right. We have a job to do, and when you're ready to finish it, I will be there should you need me."
// Page DesdemonaFree Text :
"P2670908180" "A few years back, I had an unfortunate... mishap... in dealing with my demons which cost the life of a friend, and nearly my own. After Ghost Widow saved me, I joined with Arachnos. There, I studied under the powerful Mystics of the Mu, and it was they who taught me to perform the ritual which would leave me free from potential harm at the hands of my minions. This ritual, which manifested in the tattoos you see around my neck, placed a permanent circle of protection around my mind.<br><br>It turns out that these tattoos are way more powerful than I imagined. After we beat the Avatar and I accepted the power of Vanessa's mask, something new unlocked in these tattoos, and I found that I was able to resist any form of compulsion or mind control, even one as powerful as Mother Mayhem's.<br><br>Not that it's done me a lot of good. We're still just a few people against a world of fanatical citizens, power-mad Praetors and a big, planet devouring monster. Nonetheless, I think this little plan of ours has a chance.... though it's also probably our last chance."
// DisplayName for Desdemona :

// ************************************************************************
// ************************************************************************
// ************************************************************************

