// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
// Source File : data/scripts/SpawnDefs/P_City_07_04/_src/P_City_07_04_Endgame.xls 	Sheet : NPC_Metronome 
//
// Script      : Xlstospawndef.bat 
// Version     : 38 
// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

// Script Variable Greeting :
// Script Variable Leave :

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Dialog - Metronome 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Page MetronomeIntro Text :
"P3970160967" "Greetings, {HeroName}. I am... or was... Dr. Russell Brandt, though you may call me Metronome. I am glad to finally make your acquaintance. After all, it is you I must thank for my shiny new body. Do you recognize Siege's form? All it took was some minor repairs and a fresh coat of paint to make it a worthy vessel for my mind.<br><br>But, even this new body pales in comparison to the gratitude I feel for the way you handled that wretched Dr. Keyes. I always knew him to be a madman, right up until the moment he murdered me. I wish I could have witnessed when you took his precious reactors from him. Perhaps now he knows how it feels to have your life's work taken from you.<br><br>I do wish you'd killed him, though...."
// Answer Text :
"P1484912865" "Uh, you're welcome, I guess."
// Page MetronomeProblem Text :
"P199491191" "Now then, let's say we get to the matter at hand, hmmmm?<br><br>You know our situation right now, so I won't go into that again. However, I need you to save Penelope from Tilman's clutches!"
// Answer Text :
"P2823501454" "What can we do?"
// Answer Text :
// Page MetronomeNextSteps Text :
"P3781690097" "Enter the Seer Network and free Penelope from the control of Mother Mayhem!"
// Page MetronomeAdditionalThanks Text :
"P2754268341" "Quite, quite. But, most of all, {HeroName}, I thank you for releasing Penelope Yin from the clutches of that inhuman woman. In times past, it was Penelope who believed in me, believed in the goodness that lay buried beneath the hatred that kept me alive even after my body was dead.<br><br>Though it took a solid defeat at the hands of Powers Division for me to see it, Penelope cared that my goodness be recovered... and that through it, I could be as good a man in death as I tried to be in life.<br><br>Since then, it has been my hope to rescue her from Tilman's clutches... and today, you made that hope a reality."
// Answer Text :
"P392351100" "What can we do now?"
// Answer Text :
"P3958121917" "Hopefully, Shalice Tilman will never be a threat again."
// Page MetronomeDuringAurora Text :
"P951106280" "The most pressing objective now is to finally force Tilman's Mind out into the open so it can be disconnected. As long as she remains enmeshed within the body and mind of Aurora Borealis, though, we have no hope of achieving that goal.<br><br>We are a step closer to solving that problem now, however. Once Penelope was freed, the Network cleared up enough for me to be able to perform a clear trace to Aurora's location. Desdemona will open the way. When you are in that node, however, be wary. 'Mother' has kept Aurora buried a long time. Who knows what Tilman will do to the poor girl when cornered like this.<br><br>Whatever you do... make sure Aurora survives. If her mind dies, Tilman will have full control of the body and she'll be able to turn her full attentions on us."
// Answer Text :
"P499065964" "We'll see to it that Tilman never gets that far."
// Page MetronomeDuringWell Text :
"P3021004575" "Well, that was most unexpected. Chasing Tilman from Aurora appeared to have all the effects I was thinking, but then she found the last bits of Malaise's mind rattling in the network. Those bits were enough for her to reconstitute and control his mind.<br><br>In other words, Tilman found herself a willing host to continue her work.<br><br>It's not all bad news though. Malaise's fragments weren't enough to reconstruct him perfectly, so Tilman was forced to fill in the gaps as best as she could. Since his summoning of the Nightmares was already broken in your last encounter, I would imagine that there is even less control over them and what they'll do in this state.<br><br>Perhaps that can be used to your advantage in stopping Tilman..."
// Answer Text :
"P911901507" "I'll keep that in mind. This is where it ends, Metronome."
// Page MetronomeEnding Text :
"P983097433" "One can always hope, yes. However, speaking as a disembodied mind myself, I am well aware of how pernicious such a being can be. The Seer Network is a vast, strange place where magic and science and technology collide... who knows what Tilman may have done in order to ensure she could never be destroyed?<br><br>I don't know that it matters either way, however. The two most powerful psychics are freed from her grasp and Desdemona will ensure they are protected from mind control. Even if some fragment of Tilman remains, it is likely bound to the Network for good."
// Answer Text :
"P2926351882" "We'll stop her even if she comes back. Now, what will you do?"
// Answer Text :
"P3717086963" "We'll be ready if she ever does return. <Leave>"
// Page MetronomeEnding2 Text :
"P3941682900" "What will I do? Hmmm... I think... I think I will join with Penelope and help the Resistance. We may have freed the world from that insidious Mindwashing nonsense, but we've hardly won the war. Also, to be frank, with Calvin Scott in the state he is in, I believe that it will be challenge enough for Desdemona just to hold the coalition of the Resistance together. She will need all the help she can get. I believe there are a few things I can do to assist."
// Answer Text :
"P778781772" "Thank you, Metronome. <Leave>"
// Page MetronomeFree Text :
"P2495849602" "Perhaps the presence of Siege's massive form has caused you to believe that I am something other than a disembodied mind inhabiting a robotic shell? You must remember that, at the most fundamental level, I am a mind with no body, much like Shalice Tilman herself.<br><br> Do realize, {HeroName}, that I have kept myself alive in this state by sheer force of will. So powerful and unrelenting has been my hatred and wrath in the past that it kept me going even when I should have been dead. When Penelope helped me see the goodness I could do, then the desperate mission to free her kept me going.<br><br>Try as she might, Tilman cannot mindwash me because, even with all her power, she cannot overcome my will."
// Answer Text :
"P2169456278" "I understand. Thank you, Metronome."
// DisplayName for Metronome :

// ************************************************************************
// ************************************************************************
// ************************************************************************

